# XSH aio_suspend()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The timeout is a time interval measured with CLOCK_MONOTONIC; its
# expiry is reported as EAGAIN (not ETIMEDOUT). A request that cannot
# complete is a read of an empty pipe.

assertion  XSH.aio_suspend.001
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#ERRORS/EAGAIN
class      required
since      2001
says       With one request that cannot complete and a 300 ms timeout,
           aio_suspend() returns -1 with EAGAIN, and not before 300 ms
           have passed.
test       t/001-timeout.c

assertion  XSH.aio_suspend.002
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       With a list of one pending request and one that completes (a
           file read) and a 5 s timeout, aio_suspend() returns 0 and the
           completed request is no longer in progress; the pending one
           still is.
test       t/002-one-completes.c

assertion  XSH.aio_suspend.003
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       When a request in the list has already completed, aio_suspend()
           returns 0 at once, even with a zero timeout.
test       t/003-already-done.c

assertion  XSH.aio_suspend.004
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       Null entries are ignored: a list {NULL, request, NULL} with a
           request that completes returns 0, and a list of only null
           entries with a 100 ms timeout fails with EAGAIN.
test       t/004-null-entries.c

assertion  XSH.aio_suspend.005
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       With a null timeout, aio_suspend() waits until a request
           completes (a byte is written by another thread 200 ms later) and
           returns 0, with the request no longer in progress.
test       t/005-wait-thread.c

assertion  XSH.aio_suspend.006
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#ERRORS/EINTR
anchor     functions/aio_suspend.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       A signal with a handler, sent repeatedly to the calling thread
           while it waits with no timeout on a request that cannot
           complete, makes aio_suspend() return -1 with EINTR.
test       t/006-eintr.c
